      "installed": 2000,
      "detail": "George Rickey (1907-2002), an American kinetic sculptor, built the work from two circles that remain in contact and move only by wind and gravity, without motors. Sources differ on the work's exact title: one names it 'Annular Eclipse V', while the George Rickey Foundation's public collection page names the 560 Mission Street work 'Annular Eclipse Sixteen Feet II' (1999-2000).",
      "detail_source": "res-artatsite"
    }
